{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.e0f879754935c6d04e666dfa.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Assessment concerns one SFC-authorised fund for public offering in Hong Kong; listed closed-ended alternative asset funds are excluded from this circular.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e0f879754935c6d04e666dfa.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Direct exposure, indirect exposure and NAV are measured on a consistent basis at the relevant assessment time. Their amounts are supplied as exact integers in a common accounting unit without rounding across the 50% boundary.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e0f879754935c6d04e666dfa.a2","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The measurement methodology and treatment of layered exposures must be established separately; the circular does not supply a complete calculation method.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e0f879754935c6d04e666dfa.a3","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"An operative SFC designation is a separate institutional act. Risk factors or potential scrutiny alone do not establish that designation.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.e0f879754935c6d04e666dfa.a4","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"The result identifies a complex-product classification basis under this circular, not overall distribution compliance or legal approval.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.144b125d93384c318251aa0c9a2a26d2","controlled_language":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, does the fund meet a complex-product classification basis under this circular at the assessment time? True means aggregate direct and indirect exposure is at least 50% of NAV, or an operative SFC case-specific designation exists. False means neither basis is present on established facts; it does not establish non-complex status under other requirements. Unknown inputs remain unknown unless the other branch independently establishes true. An excluded fund receives no classification conclusion from this model.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["scope"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"The mandatory 50% test aggregates direct and indirect exposure at fund level. Below 50%, the listed factors support SFC discretion rather than automatic classification; an actual designation must be distinguished from circumstances that could justify one. LAF exclusion is a scope exclusion, not a finding that the product is non-complex. Missing exposure or designation evidence remains unknown. Classification timing is also distinct from the instruction to update existing funds’ documents as soon as practicable.","run_id":"run.08f45e4d9030408999f87203f067aefc","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"be86c12a28ac1c552b9cc386dfa44174629a63a786068d9bf5d8cdb44cbfa056","source_unit_ids":["d4148dd852cee.u21.3779","d4148dd852cee.u29.4630","d4148dd852cee.u32.4805","d4148dd852cee.u4.564","d4148dd852cee.u49.6955","d4148dd852cee.u63.8691","d4148dd852cee.u64.8910"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Fund-level complex-product classification for distribution"}